### Instruction:
In a Java program, write a method to find the longest common subsequence of two strings. The method should have a time complexity of O(n^2), where n is the length of the longest input string. Additionally, the solution should not use any built-in library functions or data structures.

Rewrite the solution to use a recursive approach instead of an iterative approach.

Furthermore, implement memoization to optimize the recursive solution and reduce redundant calculations.

Additionally, modify the solution to handle multiple pairs of input strings efficiently. The method should take an array of string pairs as input and return an array of the longest common subsequences for each pair. The time complexity should still be O(n^2), where n is the length of the longest input string in each pair.

Finally, add a constraint to handle cases where the input strings can contain lowercase letters, uppercase letters, numbers, special characters, and whitespace. The method should handle such cases while maintaining the time complexity and not using any built-in library functions or data structures specifically designed for handling character comparisons.

### Response:
Here is the solution to find the longest common subsequence of two strings using an iterative approach:

```java
public class LongestCommonSubsequence {

    public static String findLCS(String str1, String str2) {
        int m = str1.length();
        int n = str2.length();

        int[][] dp = new int[m+1][n+1];

        for (int i = 0; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {
                if (i == 0 || j == 0) {
                    dp[i][j] = 0;
                } else if (str1.charAt(i-1) == str2.charAt(j-1)) {
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1;
                } else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1]);
                }
            }
        }

        int lcsLength = dp[m][n];
        char[] lcs = new char[lcsLength];

        int i = m, j = n;
        while (i > 0 && j > 0) {
            if (str1.charAt(i-1) == str2.charAt(j-1)) {
                lcs[lcsLength-1] = str1.charAt(i-1);
                i--;
                j--;
                lcsLength--;
            } else if (dp[i-1][j] > dp[i][j-1]) {
                i--;
            } else {
                j--;
            }
        }

        return new String(lcs);
    }

    public static String[] findLCS(String[][] pairs) {
        int numPairs = pairs.length;
        String[] result = new String[numPairs];

        for (int i = 0; i < numPairs; i++) {
            result[i] = findLCS(pairs[i][0], pairs[i][1]);
        }

        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String[][] pairs = {{"ABCDGH", "AEDFHR"}, {"AGGTAB", "GXTXAYB"}, {"ABCD", "ACDF"}};
        String[] lcsArray = findLCS(pairs);

        for (String lcs : lcsArray) {
            System.out.println(lcs);
        }
    }
}
```

Now let's rewrite the solution using a recursive approach:

```java
public class LongestCommonSubsequence {

    public static String findLCS(String str1, String str2) {
        int m = str1.length();
        int n = str2.length();

        if (m == 0 || n == 0) {
            return "";
        } else if (str1.charAt(m-1) == str2.charAt(n-1)) {
            return findLCS(str1.substring(0, m-1), str2.substring(0, n-1)) + str1.charAt(m-1);
        } else {
            String lcs1 = findLCS(str1.substring(0, m-1), str2);
            String lcs2 = findLCS(str1, str2.substring(0, n-1));
            return (lcs1.length() > lcs2.length()) ? lcs1 : lcs2;
        }
    }

    public static String[] findLCS(String[][] pairs) {
        int numPairs = pairs.length;
        String[] result = new String[numPairs];

        for (int i = 0; i < numPairs; i++) {
            result[i] = findLCS(pairs[i][0], pairs[i][1]);
        }

        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String[][] pairs = {{"ABCDGH", "AEDFHR"}, {"AGGTAB", "GXTXAYB"}, {"ABCD", "ACDF"}};
        String[] lcsArray = findLCS(pairs);

        for (String lcs : lcsArray) {
            System.out.println(lcs);
        }
    }
}
```

Now let's add memoization to optimize the recursive solution:

```java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class LongestCommonSubsequence {

    public static String findLCS(String str1, String str2) {
        int m = str1.length();
        int n = str2.length();

        Map<String, String> memo = new HashMap<>();

        return findLCSRecursive(str1, str2, m, n, memo);
    }

    private static String findLCSRecursive(String str1, String str2, int m, int n, Map<String, String> memo) {
        if (m == 0 || n == 0) {
            return "";
        } else if (str1.charAt(m-1) == str2.charAt(n-1)) {
            String key = m + "-" + n;
            if (!memo.containsKey(key)) {
                memo.put(key, findLCSRecursive(str1.substring(0, m-1), str2.substring(0, n-1), m-1, n-1, memo) + str1.charAt(m-1));
            }
            return memo.get(key);
        } else {
            String key1 = (m-1) + "-" + n;
            String key2 = m + "-" + (n-1);

            String lcs1 = memo.get(key1);
            if (lcs1 == null) {
                lcs1 = findLCSRecursive(str1.substring(0, m-1), str2, m-1, n, memo);
                memo.put(key1, lcs1);
            }

            String lcs2 = memo.get(key2);
            if (lcs2 == null) {
                lcs2 = findLCSRecursive(str1, str2.substring(0, n-1), m, n-1, memo);
                memo.put(key2, lcs2);
            }

            return (lcs1.length() > lcs2.length()) ? lcs1 : lcs2;
        }
    }

    public static String[] findLCS(String[][] pairs) {
        int numPairs = pairs.length;
        String[] result = new String[numPairs];

        for (int i = 0; i < numPairs; i++) {
            result[i] = findLCS(pairs[i][0], pairs[i][1]);
        }

        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String[][] pairs = {{"ABCDGH", "AEDFHR"}, {"AGGTAB", "GXTXAYB"}, {"ABCD", "ACDF"}};
        String[] lcsArray = findLCS(pairs);

        for (String lcs : lcsArray) {
            System.out.println(lcs);
        }
    }
}
```

