After calculating the `dp` array, we can find the longest common subsequence by traversing the array in reverse order. Starting from the bottom-right cell, we compare the characters at `i-1` and `j-1` with their respective previous cells in the `dp` array. If they are equal, we add the character to the `lcs` array and move diagonally up-left. Otherwise, we move up or left based on the maximum value in the adjacent cells.

